0. Preamble, My Context

i. 	In my time in the myth community on Roblox, nearing 6 years (only heavily 
passionate in recent years), I have recognized a pattern for myself, a pattern of activity 
that has me disappear for many months at a time, only to return for a few months of 
extreme inspiration, all to disappear once more. I have also noted that every time I 
return, I find a new peak for myself both in my capabilities creatively, and in my 
connections within the community. This relates not only to me being a myth, but also as 
a hunter, as I have engaged with what feels like nearly every myth out there in my time 
in the community. It is in this most recent “phase” of my engagement in the community 
that I have built up a somewhat solid idea of how the community works and the people 
and groups within the community, as well as their wants. It is this recent bout of activity 
that I have fully reached the art that I had dreamt of for so long, and have connected far 
and wide within the community. With this new perspective, I believe my concept 
of the community has reached a nice enough point to officially write out in a document, whether there 
are readers or not, and whether it holds true or not.	

ii. 	Regarding the state of the community which has given me the desire to write such 
a document, I have seen only negativity; the community has concluded that we shall
fade into nothingness. It is imperative to note, though, that the community has been on 
death’s door for many years, never truly finding death. There is an unbelievable lack of 
any conclusions in the community, though we dearly need definitions; we need to know, 
to define what we refer to as myths and myth hunters, why they both exist, how a myth 
stays unique from other art forms, and how a myth even is art. It is this sort of pursuit 
of definition that I wish to engage in here, and of course, this is by no means any attempt 
to force definitions onto the community, but a wishful start to a good concept for 
everyone to engage with. At this point in the community, only one thousand visits is
impressive, whereas one could achieve many times that amount for much less work at 
the height of the community. It is the ratio of quality games that has improved; the 
unskilled have filtered out over time, of course only rebounding after the most skilled 
had dropped the community after a certain scandal, and yet, their motives remain with 
numbers and visits. The community is aging up without sufficient rates of those entering 
the community; it is difficult to say how good this is, and I feel that those with quality 
creations might just be louder rather than larger. Regarding groups, many have gone by 
visit rankings due to the simplicity, or create forms that get reviewed for ranks, while 
others choose to rank every single new member. It all feels disconnected and like 
patchwork; the community is fractured in purpose, function, and communication.

